.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Far Navigator (ProxyFtp)


@Contents
$ #Far Navigator (ProxyFtp) (version 1.9)#

  ~Configuring client~@mnuConfigure@

  ~Work with Hosts panel~@HostPanel@

  ~Connecting to server~@ftpConnect@

  ~Work with server~@ftpCommands@

  ~Alphabetical list~@AlphaList@

@mnuConfigure
$ #Far Navigator - Configuring client#
  Before the beginning of work with Far Navigator, You need to adjust some
parameters. For entering in the configuration menu, choose #Far Navigator#
from the FAR menu #Options#/#Plugins configuration#.

  ~Interface options~@dlgInterface@    Plugin interface configuration.

  ~Connection options~@dlgConnection@   Configure ftp connection options
                      (Timeout, buffer size and etc.).

  ~Default options~@dlgDefault@      Set default host options.

  ~Proxy options~@dlgProxy@        Configure Proxy server.

  ~About Far Navigator~@dlgAbout@      Show "About..." dialog box.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@HostPanel
$ #Far Navigator - Work with Hosts panel#
  Servers list are organized in the manner of file panel. Exists two type
of entries: ~Private hosts~@HostsTypes@ and ~Public hosts~@HostsTypes@.
On Hosts Panel may use the following combinations of keys:

  #SHIFT+F4#         Create a new server entry in the
                   ~Host configuration~@dlgEdit@ dialog box.

  #F7#               Create an additional folder.

  #F4#/#SHIFT+F6#      Edit an available server entry.

  #F5#/#F6#            Copy/move a server entry from/to the local disk
                   in ~Far Navigator special file~@ftpStruct@.

  #SHIFT+F5#         Copy a host information to another record.

  #F8#               Delete a server entry/folder.

  #ENTER#            Connect to current server.

  #CTRL+G#           Connect to ~first free server from group~@GrpLogin@



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@ftpConnect
$ #Far Navigator - Connecting to server#
  You may connect to server either from command line, or through
~Hosts panel~@HostPanel@. Format for connecting from command line
to FTP server looks as follows:

  #ftp://[user[:password]@@]host[:port][/path]#

  Here prefix #ftp://# and name of server #host# are obligatory, but all rest
parameters possible not to assign (square parentheses are lowerred).
Skipped parameters Far Navigator will substitute from ~Default options~@dlgDefault@.

  If you have FAR version 1.70 or above, you also may connect to 
http server from command line. In this case format of command line looks 
as follows:

  #http://[user[:password]@@]host[:port][/path]#



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@FtpCommands
$ #Far Navigator - Work with server#
  Work with server looks like functioning with the usual local disk on
your computer. On FTP servers you may copy, delete, rename files and 
directories by means of standard combinations of keys. On HTTP servers
you may only browse folders and copy files from server. In additional, 
you may use the following combinations of keys:

  #Commands for both FTP and HTTP servers#

  #CTRL+R#     Clear internal cache and re-read panel.

  #SHIFT+F7#   Allows to change a character table for server.

  #ALT+F6#     Saves the current host and path in ~Hosts panel~@HostPanel@.

  #CTRL+ALT+S# File synchronization. As source for synchronization you 
             may use either plugin panel or file panel. (For HTTP server 
             you may use only plugin panel as source). During this process
             plugin will copy all new/updated files from source panel.
             On destination panel will be deleted all obsoleted files.

  #FTP server commands#

  #CTRL+A#     Displays a menu of changing the access rights or owner.
                                                                    
  #CTRL+S#     Translate command line to FTP server.

  #SHIFT+F5#   Copy files in ~Server To Server transfer mode~@S2S@.

  #ALT+F5#     All selected files will be added in ~Download queue~@DnQueue@

  #F3 on ".."# Shows FTP server welcome message

  #F5 on ".."# If you have no selected files on panel, You will be
             asked for filename to copy. In this case you must enter
             _full_ filename without mask chars.
                                                           
  You can use ~Advanced mode~@dlgAdvanced@ to copy/move/delete files.

  Also you may use additional item in plugins menu (called by F11):
~Far Navigator - Synchronization~@Synchronization@



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgInterface
$ #Far Navigator - Interface options#
  In this dialogue you adjust external parameters of Far Navigator. You may:

 - Add Far Navigator in the menu of choice of disks;
 - Create descriptions files list, dilimited with comma; 
 - Switch On/Off a reading the files descriptions and their automatic
   renovation;
 - Set [connect] as default button
   in the ~Host configuration~@dlgEdit@ dialog box.
 - "Show progress indicator on View/Edit" will display Progress bar
   when plugin retrieves files for View/Edit

 ~Advanced options~@dlgIntAdv@


  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgIntAdv
$ #ProxyFtp - Advanced interface options#
                                                       
 - "Replace Panel mode 0" will set Panel mode 0 (Called on LCtrl+0)
   on FTP server to view custom columns you defined. In addition,
   you may customize "file panel view modes" using special "column
   types":
   #C0#: Access mode
   #C1#: File owner
   #C2#: File group
   #C3#: Real destination name for file links



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgAbout
$ #ProxyFtp - About#
  In this dialog box possible to find some information on the program
and on its author. All wish and offer you may send to:

     e-mail:  #proxykit@@newmail.ru#

       fido:  #2:5004/18.32@@fidonet.org#

        ICQ:  #17217849#

  Home page:  #http://www.angelfire.com/me/vmoshninov#



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgConnection
$ #ProxyFtp - Connection options#
  This dialogue is intended for configuring of network connection between
the client and FTP server. Here available the following options:

  #Log file name#     Full path with filename of log file.

  #Create log file#   Set this option if you want to create log file.
  #Log file level#    Set level for log file:
                    0 - Minimal level, 3 - Maximal level
                      
  #Connection#        Timeout (in seconds) on any socket operation
  #timeout#           (connecting to server, receiving and sending
                    data). After timeout expired, ProxyFtp will break
                    operation, try reconnect and resume operation.
                                            
  #Idle timeout#      Timeout (in seconds), after which client will
                    send on the server "empty" command for preventing
                    a disconnecting.

  #Quick logout#      In this mode plugin does not wait for reply on
                    logout.

  #Write ftp cache#   All cached dirs on ftp servers can be stored to
  #to disk#           your hard drive for future use. When you are
                    connected to the server in the next time, all cached
                    dirs will be restored.                         

  All attempts of connecting (or reconnecting) are divided into groups.
You may adjust several parameters to indicate how ProxyFtp must be connected
to the server.

  #Maximum Retries#   Retries count before ProxyFtp will display error
  #count#             message (0 - never expired)

  #Timeout between#   This parameter define timeout between two groups
  #two Retries group# of attempts of connecting to the server

  #Retries count in#  Retries count in group of attempts of connecting.
  #group#

  #Retries timeout#   Retries timeout in group of attempts of
  #in group#          connecting.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgProxy
$ #ProxyFtp - Proxy options#
  This dialog box allows configure your client to functioning through FTP
or HTTP Proxy server. The following parameters are available:

  #Proxy server#      Will here be assigned address and port of Proxy
                    in the format #[user@@]proxy[:port]# Address of
                    server #proxy# is an obligatory parameter, all rest
                    are optioonal.

  #Password#          Password for HTTP Proxy server.

  #Proxy style#       Set your Proxy server style.
                                              
  #Do HTTP basic#     Set this option if your HTTP proxy requires that
  #authorization#     you were registered.

  #Use HTTP cache#    Set this option if you want that your HTTP
                      proxy uses cache.

  #HTTP Proxy type#   Select type of your http proxy. Now available:
                    #Microsoft Proxy server#
                    #WinGate proxy server#
                    #Novell BorderManager#
                    #SquId proxy server#
                    #Netscape proxy server#
                    #WinProxy#



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgDefault
$ #ProxyFtp - Default options#
  In this dialogue you will assign parameters, which are used when connecting
either from ~Command line~@ftpConnect@ or through ~Hosts panel~@HostPanel@.

  #User name#         Will assign an user name, which is sent on FTP
                    server when connecting, unless given main.

  Values of rest parameters comply with values of similar parameters from
dialogue ~Host configuration~@dlgEdit@.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgEdit
$ #ProxyFtp - Editing FTP server#
  This dialogue is intended for entering and adjustment information on FTP
server. Here you may assign the following parameters:

  #Server#            Here you will assign an address FTP server.

  #Password#          Password for FTP server, if it necessary.

  #Account#           If for connecting to your FTP server it is
                    necessary to indicate a resource, you may assign
                    its here.

  #Description#       Small description of FTP server.

  #Ask password#      When installing this options a password dialog 
  #before connection# will be called before the connection.

  #Passive mode#      Work with FTP server in "passive" mode.

  #ASCII mode#        Use ASCII Transfer mode for files. (Text files)

  #Use proxy#         Set this option if are required to use Proxy
                    server for this host.

  #Chracter table#    Select character table for this host.
                                                                
  #FTP server type#   Select type of FTP server. In some cases
                    ProxyFtp can't recognize server automatically and
                    you must define this parameter manually. This
                    parameter uses for parsing FTP server listings.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@ftpStruct
$ #ProxyFtp - Special file#
  This file is used for keeping information about FTP server on the local disk
and presents textual .ini file from itself. Looks such file approximately as
follows:

 [ProxyFTP]
 URL=ftp://rwntug.quarta.msk.ru/winutil/rar/farplugin
 Description=FAR plugins
 Account=
 Ask password=0
 Password=
 Passive mode=0
 Ascii mode=0
 Use proxy=1
 TableID=-4
 SystemId=206

  You may edit this file in the standard text editor, write such file on
~Hosts panel~@HostPanel@ or connect to FTP server by pressing ENTER on such
file.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@S2S
$ #ProxyFtp - "Server To Server" transfer mode#
  Interaction Scheme with FTP server looks as follows:

     +--------+     Control connection     +--------+
     | Client | <------------------------> | Server |
     +--------+                            +--------+
          ^---------  Data connection  --------^

  #Control connection# stays to be openned during the whole session of
functioning with FTP server and uses for the sending of commands and
receiving of answers. #Data connection# is openned for the transmission/receiving
the files only and is then closed newly. Under simultaneous functioning with
two FTP servers possible to organizine a #Server to server transfer mode#. In
this case interaction scheme looks as follows:

     +--------+       Data connection      +--------+
     | Server | <------------------------> | Server |
     +--------+                            +--------+
          |             +--------+             |
          +------------ | Client | ------------+
     Control            +--------+            Control
     connection                            connection

  Such scheme suitable in that event, if channel between servers of quicker
channel from the server to client.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@AlphaList                                  
$ #ProxyFtp - Alphabetical list#

  ~About ProxyFtp~@dlgAbout@
  ~Advanced interface options~@dlgIntAdv@
  ~Advanced copy/move/delete mode~@dlgAdvanced@
  ~Configuring FTP client~@mnuConfigure@
  ~Connection options~@dlgConnection@
  ~Connection to FTP server~@ftpConnect@
  ~Default options~@dlgDefault@
  ~Download queue~@DnQueue@
  ~Group connection~@GrpLogin@
  ~Host configuration~@dlgEdit@
  ~Interface options~@dlgInterface@
  ~Rename files~@dlgRename@
  ~Private hosts and public hosts~@HostsTypes@
  ~Proxy options~@dlgProxy@
  ~ProxyFTP special file~@ftpStruct@
  ~ProxyFtp - Synchronization~@Synchronization@
  ~Server To Server transfer mode~@S2S@
  ~Work with FTP server~@ftpCommands@
  ~Work with Hosts panel~@HostPanel@



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgAdvanced
$ #ProxyFtp - Advanced copy/move/delete mode#

  In this mode you can process files with specified mask (#Include mask#),
skip some files from operation (#Exclude mask#) or decode/encode group of files
"on the fly".

 #Remote character table# is the charset of files on FTP server.
 #Local character table#  is the charset of files on local machine.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@dlgRename
$ #ProxyFtp - Rename files#

 #Use quick renaming for folders# - in this mode a client will use for
folders renaming of command RNFR/RNTO. Otherwise will use recursive
renaming for each subfolders and files in this folder.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@HostsTypes
$ #ProxyFtp - Private hosts and public hosts#

 By default in root of ~Hosts panel~@HostPanel@ you have two directory:
#Private hosts# and #Public hosts#. All entries, created in 'Private hosts'
will be stored in separate (private) key of registry and not copied with
standard SaveSettings.bat and RestoreSettings.bat FAR batch files.
If you don't want to use 'Private hosts', you must disable "Show 'Private Hosts'
in Hosts panel" in ~Interface options~@dlgInterface@.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@DnQueue
$ #ProxyFtp - Download queue#
 You may use #Download queue# for storing files for copying instead of
real downloading from FTP server. When you mark all files for copying, you may
switch to 'Download queue' and start downloading. To add files in
'Download queue' you may press #ALT+F5# or press #[Queue]# button in 'Copy'
dialogue. #CTRL+SHIFT+F5# will switch between normal FTP mode and
Download queue. In Download queue you mau use #F8# for deleting files from
queue, #F5#/#F6# for start downloading.
#F6 will move files only from queue, not from FTP server!#.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@GrpLogin
$ #ProxyFtp - Group connection#
 When you have selected files in ~Hosts panel~@HostPanel@ and press #CTRL+G#, ProxyFtp
begin attempt to connect to first free server from group. If first server
from group fails, ProxyFtp will try second, then third, e.t.c When last server
fails, ProxyFtp go to first server and will try again.



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@Synchronization
$ #ProxyFtp - Synchronization#
  If you on local disk and select this item, ProxyFtp will scan for
~proxyftp.mnu~@ftpStruct@ file in current directory and all above. If
file exists, ProxyFtp will read from this file information about ftp
servers, connect to the server (if many - will appear menu) and
go to the same folder as local dir. Current directory will appear
on another panel. Folder with 'proxyftp.mnu' file will 'root'.    
  After you connected to the server, you may synchronize active and
inactive panels by calling this menuitem again. Path on inactive panel
will synchronize with path on active panel.

Special thanks to PAF (Alexander Petrosyan) for idea.


  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@
